From ebe271bc2cb4967d0562b3bbfb061d1eca712f76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:25:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] selftests/bpf: exercise the CPUMAP RFS policy with real
 sockets

Compile the sample BPF source into the test object and observe actual
stack handoff from TC. Use TCP and connected UDP sockets over IPv4/IPv6
to check receive/send CPU changes, accept/splice/zero-copy observers,
MSG_ERRQUEUE exclusion, absent and outside-set hints, and socket
recreation. Check both the receiving CPU and payload order.

Inject native XDP UDP frames into live sockets to cover the native
CPUMAP delivery path. Configure the private namespace to accept injected
loopback traffic without a cached output route. Check lookup-miss
redirect and the parser's unsupported/truncated packet boundary.

Existing ordered CPUMAP tests cover the migration barrier, queue-full,
concurrent producers, target replacement and CPU hotplug separately.
Run on an x86-64 CONFIG_RPS=n kernel with KASAN and lockdep enabled.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
